"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds–Karp, rather than Dinic, because each of its steps is one picture: a shortest path in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the residual network and the flow sent along it. Dinic’s blocking flows interleave advancing,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retreating and pruning within a level graph, which do not read as separate steps."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Making the sequence numbers the vertices and reads the capacities as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"edmondsKarpMaximumFlow(from:to:capacity:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does; each iterator builds its own residual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"network and runs that call’s searches, in the same order, so the flows it sends are that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call’s: the pushes less the cancellations on each edge are its ","type":"text"},{"code":"flow(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bottlenecks add up to its ","type":"text"},{"code":"value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The sequence holds no copy of the graph; its positions stay","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"valid until the graph is mutated. Stopping the loop stops the algorithm.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/ST"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/edmondskarpevents"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvents\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/